{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>I will go</b> — to myself, with none pursuing after me. Or: I will go with the prey. And the correct interpretation is: I will tear them and go to myself, as is written after it." "<b>Until they bear guilt</b> — that they acknowledge they are guilty. Or like the meaning of \"שממה תשים שומרון\" (Samaria shall become a desolation). And \"והאדמה לא תשם\" is deficient alef." "<b>They will seek Me</b> — they will seek Me at dawn, and say, each to each: \"Come.\" He said \"טרף\" (prey) on account of \"ככפיר\" (like a young lion)."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The phrase והאדמה לא תשם is a cross-reference to a defective spelling of תשם elsewhere (likely Hosea 10:2 or similar); the point is that תשם there lacks an alef, i.e., תשם not תאשם, which affects whether the root is שום or אשם."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:21.514558295Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}